  "verdict": {
    "kind": "move-after",
    "label": "Ready after 4 changes",
    "title": "You can move node-railway to Cloud Run after 4 changes",
    "reason": "The timers, the sessions in memory, the files on disk and the worker need a change each before Cloud Run; the rest moves as it is."
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "i": 1,
      "id": "in-process-timer",
      "kind": "breaks",
      "title": "Timers inside the process",
      "at": "src/clock.js:9",
      "code": "cron.schedule('0 * * * *', cleanup);",
      "why": "A service at zero has no process to run a timer, a running one gets no CPU between requests, and with several instances the timer fires once per instance: late, never, or twice.",
      "fix": "Cloud Scheduler on the same cron lines: short work calls POST /cron/<name> on the service with an OIDC token, long work starts a Cloud Run job. Set each job's time zone; the timer ran on the server's, usually UTC.",
      "part": "clock",
      "kb": "cron-and-timers-with-cloud-scheduler",
      "subject": "the timers",
      "task": 2
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "id": "memory-sessions",
      "kind": "breaks",
      "title": "Sessions kept in process memory",
      "at": "src/server.js:14",
      "code": "app.use(session({ secret: process.env.SESSION_SECRET, resave: false, saveUninitialized: false }));",
      "why": "Each instance has its own memory and loses it when it stops, so a user is signed out whenever a request lands on another instance or a new one.",
      "fix": "Signed cookies (cookie-session), with the key in Secret Manager.",
      "part": "web",
      "kb": "sessions-without-redis",
      "subject": "the sessions in memory",
      "task": 3
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "id": "local-disk-write",
      "kind": "breaks",
      "title": "Files written to local disk",
      "at": "src/server.js:30",
      "code": "await fs.writeFile(path.join(UPLOAD_DIR, name), req.file.buffer);",
      "why": "An instance's disk lives in its memory: a file counts against the memory limit, is gone when the instance stops, and other instances never see it, so an upload saved on one is a 404 on the next.",
      "fix": "Write to a Cloud Storage bucket and hand out signed URLs; for uploads, let the browser PUT the file to a signed URL so the bytes never pass through the service.",
      "part": "uploads",
      "kb": "files-and-uploads-with-cloud-storage",
      "subject": "the files on disk",
      "task": 4
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "id": "queue-worker",
      "kind": "breaks",
      "title": "A worker waits on a Redis queue",
      "at": "src/worker.js:9",
      "code": "new Worker('jobs', handle, { connection: redis });",
      "why": "Cloud Run gives an instance CPU only while it answers a request, so a worker waiting on a queue gets no CPU between requests and its jobs stall. With CPU always allocated it runs, and bills every second whether there is work or not.",
      "fix": "Cloud Tasks: where the code adds a job, it creates a task that POSTs to /tasks/<name> on the service, and a handler there does the job and answers 2xx. Retries, backoff and rate limits move to the queue; check the OIDC token and make the handler safe to run twice.",
      "part": "worker",
      "kb": "background-workers-with-cloud-tasks",
      "subject": "the worker",
      "task": 5
    }
  ],
